  "published": "2026-07-01T15:25:03.643Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 4.2.1. Fixes a latent hang: a UseTimeProvider(factory) whose factory resolves TimeProvider from the service provider (e.g. sp.GetService<TimeProvider>()) is a self-referential registration — that factory IS the TimeProvider registration, so resolving TimeProvider inside it recursed until the DI container deadlocked. It only surfaced when something first resolved the clock, so tests injecting a clock directly never caught it. The factory is now guarded and fails fast with a clear message instead. To make CQRSharp defer to a TimeProvider your host already registered, don't call UseTimeProvider at all: AddCqrs registers TimeProvider.System with TryAdd, so an existing registration wins.",
